// What csp_fprint_value does with the value_t ARMS, which is a dump concern and
// not a semantic one -- so nothing else in the suite looks at it.
//
// It printed val.i for V_DIGITAL, V_ANALOG and V_TIMER: the union's whole word,
// which for a digital carries cfg/pin/port/dir/pullup above the value bit and
// so reported a lit pin as a large number. Reading it back through a rule still
// worked, which is why the bug lived in the listing alone.
//
// Of 77 expect files exactly one (dio) checked a pin at all, so this is the
// regression test for the arms rather than for the behaviour.

#digital Led    out 13
#analog  Dac:10 out 0:2
#timer   T      1000
#variable N = 0

N = N + 1 ? N < 4
Led = 1 ? N > 1
Dac = 300 ? N > 1
T = 1 ? N > 1
